usage: query_profile.py [-h] --input INPUT --output OUTPUT [--summary-only]
                        [--large-capture] [--allow-unmapped-event-labels]

Offline measureme 12.0.3 MMPD format-9 raw-event decoder. Primary layout
sources: measureme 12.0.3 file_header.rs, serialization.rs, stringtable.rs and
raw_event.rs. decodeme 10.1.3 supplies label semantics only: its older 32-bit
string/index layout is NOT format 9 and is not used here. Import decode(bytes)
-> list[dict]. Records retain their original numeric 64-bit event_id, with
kind/label resolved separately. Virtual IDs <=100000000 can be correlated with
the recording invocation's DepNodeIndex, never across invocations. Raw
timestamps are relative counter values in nanoseconds, with no epoch offset,
DAG inference, exclusive CPU-work or span interpretation.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --input INPUT
  --output OUTPUT
  --summary-only        validate all raw records but write compact
                        counts/hash/metadata instead of event JSON
  --large-capture       opt in to 8M events/4M string mappings; 256MiB byte
                        bound unchanged
  --allow-unmapped-event-labels
                        retain missing user-virtual event labels as null with
                        label_resolved=false
